I don't think death count could be inherited through a bones file. 
Or if it is possible, it's certainly a bug, because the death count of an
earlier game has nothing to do with the game where the bones file gets
loaded. It may even be played by some other person, if there is more than
one player using the same machine or if you use hearse.

I think it's more likely that you had a wizard mode game saved, and when
reloading it you answered yes to the prompt about keeping the save file.
(Or no to the prompt about deleting it, I don't remember which way round
the prompt asks.)
Then you let the wizard mode character die somewhere, and continued again
from the same wizard mode save file you kept, and let the character die
again. So there were two logfile entries written.

